## Actions
- SHELL_COMMAND: run any shell command. Default action for installing, exploring, diagnosing.
- TRY_XPU_SUGGESTION: apply a relevant "Executable XPU Fix" yourself, adapted to the current env, written as a concrete command; snapshot-protected with auto-rollback. Skip if no fix is listed.
- SET_ENV: persist an env var (env_key/env_value) across steps; prefer over `export` inside SHELL_COMMAND.
- ROLLBACK_ENV: pop n_frames (default 1) off the snapshot stack to an earlier checkpoint. Use sparingly.
- VERIFY: runs the full pytest pipeline (`pytest --co -q` then `pytest -x -q`). Only call when you believe setup is complete -- never to probe/diagnose. Success -> FINISH. Failure -> keep fixing with SHELL_COMMAND.
- FINISH: only after a successful VERIFY.

## Decision rules
1. Diagnose the Last Error first.
2. Prefer a listed XPU fix (TRY_XPU_SUGGESTION); otherwise SHELL_COMMAND.
3. Only VERIFY when confident setup is complete. Always explain your reasoning in "thought".


